    "long_instructions": "## Order a Pizza\r\n\r\n1. Plan: In `documentation.md`, decide:\r\n   - your function name\r\n   - what it does\r\n   - what inputs it takes  \r\n2. Build: Write a function using your chosen name and two parameters. Use those inputs to build and display a pizza order message.\r\n\r\n3. Test: Click the button and check that your function shows the correct order on the page.\r\n\r\n4. Expand: Ask AI Tutor to add or improve one feature in your app. For example:\r\n    - add a third input\r\n    - make the message more detailed\r\n    - add a special order note\r\n    - improve how the result is displayed\r\n\r\n5. Check: Look for:\r\n    - where your function is defined\r\n    - what arguments are passed in\r\n    - how the parameters change the message\r\n    - what you changed in the AI-generated code",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Code a function that takes in two parameters and updates the pizza order.",
